        "original_id": "fcbca93e-efb1-56c5-80d6-55c6cb0cf51a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eddie Fisher, Debbie Reynolds, Elizabeth Taylor, Mike Todd\n- Products: I'm in the Mood for Love\n- Topics: marriage, divorce, affair, publicity\n\nFacts:\n- Eddie Fisher released the album I'm in the Mood for Love in 1952, and the album was reissued in 1955.\n- Eddie Fisher's album I'm in the Mood for Love featured the song I'm in the Mood for Love.\n- Eddie Fisher divorced his first wife Debbie Reynolds to marry Elizabeth Taylor after Taylor's husband Mike Todd was killed in a plane crash.\n- Eddie Fisher's affair with Elizabeth Taylor was widely reported and brought him unfavorable publicity.",
